<title>UK: Bad weather closes two Italian ports - ship brokers.</title>
<headline>Bad weather closes two Italian ports - ship brokers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bad weather has closed the Italian ports of Fiumicino and Falconara, shipping sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Fiumicino has been closed since last week and Falconara for a couple of days,&quot; one tanker broker said, adding it was currently too risky for vessels to berth safely.</p>
<p>He said he did not know when the ports were likely to reopen and had no more details.</p>
<p>Another broker said he thought Algeria's Skikda port had also closed briefly due to bad weather but was now open again. He had no more details.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
